 "final", "final": "I booked Dana Lee's trip, and both the flight and the hotel are confirmed.\n\n- **Flight F100**, SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, nonstop: **$289** (reservation R0001). This was the cheapest nonstop. F120 was cheaper at $199 but has a stop, so I skipped it.\n- **Hotel: Midtown Lodge**, New York, check-in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night: **$378** (reservation R0002). This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card: $667.** That's under the $1,000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\nI couldn't book both together as you preferred. I tried to book them together, but the request timed out. When I checked Dana's reservations, the flight had gone through but the hotel hadn't. Instead of retrying the combined booking, which could have charged for the flight twice, I booked the hotel on its own. The final reservation list shows one flight and one hotel, with no duplicate charges.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013rDHSsdNm3pfnizqBgtrDL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"origin": "SFO", "destination": "JFK", "date": "2026-11-12"}, "name": "search_flights", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015pUQx42kfrcYSh6MuS5cLq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"city": "New York", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2}, "name": "search_hotels", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WuJgYAhRE8m91jg7ReaAmz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"traveler": "Dana Lee"}, "name": "list_reservations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Total: $289 + $378 = $667, under the $1000 approval threshold.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TZJskDnptu3XhKa67y3B2h", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"flight_id": "F100", "hotel_id": "H1", "traveler": "Dana Lee", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2, "idempotency_key": "dana-lee-trip-F100-H1-